# Files the iyi port refuses in the declarations pass, with why: <repo-relative file> <reason>.
# The gate fails a file the port refuses unless it is listed here, and fails a listed file the port no
# longer refuses (remove its row then). A listed file counts the 0 its floor row holds.
#
# The LLVM bridge declares `lib ::LibLLVM` inside one `{% begin %}` block. Its VERSION constant is
# `llvm_version.strip.gsub(/git/, "").gsub(/-?rc.*/, "")`. The port's macro engine has `StringLiteral#strip` but no
# regex, so no `StringLiteral#gsub`, and the block does not declare the lib. Every file that names a LibLLVM type
# is refused with "undefined constant LibLLVM::<Type>".
src/compiler/backend/llvm/emit.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/backend/llvm/import.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/backend/llvm/translate.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/builder.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/context.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/llvm.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/memory_buffer.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/module.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/pass_manager.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/target.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/llvm/values.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
src/compiler/tools/ir.iyi the LibLLVM lib is not declared: the macro engine does not port StringLiteral#gsub (regex)
# A file analysed bare has no prelude. The port follows this file's import of compiler/tools/formatter and resolves
# that unit's `Set`, a prelude type, while it declares the file; the hosted pass declares the file bare. With the
# prelude loaded (entry mode) both sides print the same 3 declarations.
src/compiler/tools/format.iyi undefined constant Set: analysed bare, the port resolves a prelude type named by the imported compiler/tools/formatter
